Comprehensive Project Report: AgriGuard AI
Executive Summary
AgriGuard AI is an end-to-end, climate-smart agricultural advisory platform engineered to provide smallholder farmers,
extension officers, and agricultural institutions in India with real-time, data-driven farming intelligence.
By combining a hybrid ensemble AI pipeline (T5-PEFT, Climate-LoRA, Ollama, Groq), domain-specific historical advisory databases, 
real-time weather integration (OpenMeteo, NASA POWER), and heuristic soil scoring, AgriGuard AI delivers hyper-localized,
actionable crop advisories across multiple Indian languages.
1. Brainstorming and Ideation
Problem Statement: Indian smallholder farmers face severe crop yield degradation due to climate variability, 
unpredictable weather shifts, degraded soil health, and fragmented advisory services that lack hyper-local specificity and regional language accessibility.

Proposed Solution: A modular, multilingual decision-support system that processes farmer location, NPK nutrient values, 
and soil pH alongside live 7-day weather forecasts and 10-year historical climate trends to generate actionable farming advisories under one minute.
2. Requirement Analysis
Functional Requirements
Location & Soil Inputs: Capture state, district, crop type, Nitrogen (N), Phosphorus (P), Potassium (K), and soil pH.

Weather Intelligence: Automatically fetch real-time forecasts, temperature trends, and humidity levels via OpenMeteo API.

Heuristic Scoring Engine: Calculate crop suitability indices and climate risk scores (drought, flood, heat stress).

Multilingual Advisory Generation: Synthesize advisories in Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Marathi, Punjabi, and English with voice output support.

Audit Trail & Data Export: Log queries in session memory/database with one-click JSON and CSV dataset exporting.

Non-Functional Requirements
Performance & Latency: Core pipeline response time under 3 seconds; audio summarization under 1 minute.

Scalability: Modular Python-based service architecture supporting both local edge inference (Ollama) and high-speed cloud APIs (Groq).

Usability: Mobile-responsive, low-friction Streamlit dashboard tailored for non-technical agricultural extension workers.
